      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 4.591,
          "en": "Now that we got the getAllPosts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.591,
          "end": 7.76,
          "en": "and getFeaturedPosts functions, let's use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.76,
          "end": 9.91,
          "en": "For example, on the starting page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.91,
          "end": 14.27,
          "en": "so that there we can get rid of that DUMMY_POSTS array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.27,
          "end": 17.92,
          "en": "and instead we load posts from our own data source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.92,
          "end": 21.02,
          "en": "And when it comes to fetching data for a page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.02,
          "end": 23.51,
          "en": "we also learned how that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.51,
          "end": 28.24,
          "en": "We wanna use getStaticProps or getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.24,
          "end": 31.8,
          "en": "In reality, of course, we don't need either of the two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 36.43,
          "en": "We could also use useEffect inside of our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.43,
          "end": 40.33,
          "en": "and send an HTTP request to some API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.33,
          "end": 42.88,
          "en": "But that means that the pre-rendered page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.88,
          "end": 45.1,
          "en": "won't contain any content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.1,
          "end": 47.21,
          "en": "which isn't great for search engines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.21,
          "end": 49.72,
          "en": "and in this specific website here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.72,
          "end": 51.76,
          "en": "we would also have a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.76,
          "end": 54,
          "en": "We have no API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54,
          "end": 56.93,
          "en": "Our posts are fetched from the file system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.93,
          "end": 59.8,
          "en": "And we can therefore do that in any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.8,
          "end": 62.05,
          "en": "that runs on the server side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.05,
          "end": 64.12,
          "en": "and has access to that file system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.12,
          "end": 66.84,
          "en": "but we can't do it from inside our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.84,
          "end": 69.68,
          "en": "Those don't have access to the file system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.68,
          "end": 73,
          "en": "and there, we also can't send a request to any API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73,
          "end": 74.57,
          "en": "that grants that access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.57,
          "end": 77.28999999999999,
          "en": "because we have no such API here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.28999999999999,
          "end": 79.4,
          "en": "We could build an API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.4,
          "end": 81.36,
          "en": "but why would we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.36,
          "end": 83.65,
          "en": "Then we would be able to fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.65,
          "end": 85.67,
          "en": "without having it pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.67,
          "end": 89.43,
          "en": "and we would still have the search engine disadvantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.43,
          "end": 92.4,
          "en": "Therefore, it definitely makes most sense here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.4,
          "end": 96.16,
          "en": "to add the separate getStaticProps function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.81,
          "end": 103.8,
          "en": "In here, we wanna get all the featured posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.8,
          "end": 105.4,
          "en": "and that's super simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.4,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "because in that lib folder in which we just worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 112.72,
          "en": "in that file there, we export a getFeaturedPosts function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.72,
          "end": 114.77000000000001,
          "en": "which does just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.77000000000001,
          "end": 116.72999999999999,
          "en": "So here in getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "we can get our featuredPosts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 119.87,
          "en": "by calling getFeaturedPosts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.41,
          "end": 122.9,
          "en": "And you just need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.9,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "that you add a import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 127.99,
          "en": "importing getFeaturedPosts from that lib folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.99,
          "end": 129.713,
          "en": "and the posts-util file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 133.63,
          "en": "If you do that, you've got the featuredPosts here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.63,
          "end": 136.03,
          "en": "and then you learned earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.03,
          "end": 137.77,
          "en": "that in getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.77,
          "end": 140.87,
          "en": "we should return an object with a props key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.87,
          "end": 144.52,
          "en": "where we then can pass any props of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.52,
          "end": 145.89,
          "en": "to the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.89,
          "end": 147.34,
          "en": "Now, here I guess it makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.34,
          "end": 152.34,
          "en": "to set a posts prop, which holds those loaded featuredPosts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.77,
          "end": 156.49,
          "en": "And that's already all we have to do in getStaticProps here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.49,
          "end": 159.94,
          "en": "Nothing else is required for this use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.94,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "Now, we could also be using getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.85,
          "end": 168.11,
          "en": "to always fetch all the featuredPosts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.11,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "when a request reaches this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "but that doesn't make sense here I would say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 175.13,
          "en": "It will just slow down this page a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.13,
          "end": 177.65,
          "en": "because we have to go through all the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.65,
          "end": 180.78,
          "en": "and go through all the posts for every request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.78,
          "end": 182.41,
          "en": "without gaining much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.41,
          "end": 186.66,
          "en": "Our posts will probably not change every second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.66,
          "end": 189.476,
          "en": "After all, we have to change our Markdown file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.476,
          "end": 191.81,
          "en": "to update them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.81,
          "end": 194.13,
          "en": "So they are fairly stable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 194.13,
          "end": 197.25,
          "en": "Most posts will probably never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "So getStaticProps makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 203.21,
          "en": "Now, we could add the revalidate key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.21,
          "end": 205.96,
          "en": "to make it clear that getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.96,
          "end": 210.16,
          "en": "should not just be executed once during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 210.16,
          "end": 214.39,
          "en": "as you learned but also at least once every 100 seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.39,
          "end": 217.13,
          "en": "or every 60 seconds or whatever you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.13,
          "end": 219.81,
          "en": "for a new incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 222.8,
          "en": "This would ensure that if our data changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.8,
          "end": 227.18,
          "en": "after deployment, we still regenerate our posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.18,
          "end": 230.2,
          "en": "and we therefore reflect that latest data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.2,
          "end": 233.62,
          "en": "without rebuilding and redeploying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 233.62,
          "end": 235.5,
          "en": "We could do that but again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.5,
          "end": 238.82999999999998,
          "en": "our posts will probably not change that much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.82999999999998,
          "end": 240.96,
          "en": "So if you wanna set revalidate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.96,
          "end": 244.26,
          "en": "to have that built-in rebuilding step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.26,
          "end": 247.72,
          "en": "you wanna definitely set it to a long duration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 247.72,
          "end": 252.13,
          "en": "maybe 10 minutes or even longer, like half an hour",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 252.13,
          "end": 254.92,
          "en": "and here I will not set it at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.92,
          "end": 256.75,
          "en": "which means getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.75,
          "end": 260.67,
          "en": "will only be executed once outside of development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 265.67,
          "en": "during development it will be executed for every request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.22,
          "end": 267.94,
          "en": "but outside of development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 267.94,
          "end": 271.36,
          "en": "it will only be executed when we build the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 271.36,
          "end": 274.18,
          "en": "for production and never thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.18,
          "end": 277.03,
          "en": "And I would say this is absolutely fine here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.03,
          "end": 278.663,
          "en": "for this scenario.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 279.67,
          "end": 283.09000000000003,
          "en": "Okay, so now with that, we have getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.09000000000003,
          "end": 284.95,
          "en": "we set the posts prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 284.95,
          "end": 286.88,
          "en": "which holds the featuredPosts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 286.88,
          "end": 288.82,
          "en": "and that means that in HomePage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 288.82,
          "end": 290.33,
          "en": "we should accept props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 290.33,
          "end": 294.37,
          "en": "and then pass props.posts as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 294.37,
          "end": 296.98,
          "en": "to the posts prop on FeaturedPosts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 299.897,
          "en": "If you now save all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 299.897,
          "end": 302.8,
          "en": "and we go back to the starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 302.8,
          "end": 306.83,
          "en": "there we should see one featured post now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 306.83,
          "end": 310.16,
          "en": "and now here, the data is actually coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 310.16,
          "end": 312.35,
          "en": "from our Markdown file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 312.35,
          "end": 315.39,
          "en": "So if I change something there like the date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 315.39,
          "end": 318.36,
          "en": "from 15th to 16th,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 318.36,
          "end": 320.41,
          "en": "then since we're in development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 320.41,
          "end": 324.41,
          "en": "and getStaticProps runs for every request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 324.41,
          "end": 325.96,
          "en": "when we'll see that if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 325.96,
          "end": 329.32,
          "en": "this switched to 16th as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 329.32,
          "end": 332.43,
          "en": "So this data is coming from the Markdown file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 332.43,
          "end": 334.4,
          "en": "And now we can do something similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 334.4,
          "end": 336.63,
          "en": "in the All Posts page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 336.63,
          "end": 339.47,
          "en": "Of course, feel free to try this on your own first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 339.47,
          "end": 341.31,
          "en": "Here is your chance to pause the video",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.31,
          "end": 343.31,
          "en": "and try it on your own first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 343.31,
          "end": 345.823,
          "en": "After a short pause, we'll implement it together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 349.63,
          "end": 351.3,
          "en": "Were you successful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 351.3,
          "end": 355.46500000000003,
          "en": "Let's implement it together on that All Posts page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 355.46500000000003,
          "end": 358.71,
          "en": "There it's very similar to the starting page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 358.71,
          "end": 361.3,
          "en": "So here in posts, index.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 361.3,
          "end": 363.89,
          "en": "we don't wanna use the DUMMY_POSTS any more,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 363.89,
          "end": 365.99,
          "en": "we wanna get rid of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 365.99,
          "end": 370.44,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna fetch posts from our actual data source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 370.44,
          "end": 372.953,
          "en": "And again, for this, I'll use getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 374.251,
          "end": 377.77,
          "en": "So I'll export a function getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 377.77,
          "end": 379.75,
          "en": "to fetch my posts here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 379.75,
          "end": 383.5,
          "en": "Again, getServerSideProps makes no sense for me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 383.5,
          "end": 387.04,
          "en": "because we don't want to fetch all the posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 387.04,
          "end": 388.63,
          "en": "for every request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 388.63,
          "end": 391.63,
          "en": "That would not be that great for performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 391.63,
          "end": 394.33,
          "en": "Instead, doing it once during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
